AIM: Develop programs for implementing plots with matplotlib. 
 
1) Creating a vertical bar chart 
SOURCE CODE: 
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt 
x= ['one','two','three','four','five'] 
y = [5,24,35,67,12] 
plt.bar(x,y) 
plt.xlabel("Pen sold") 
plt.ylabel("Price") 
plt.title("Vertical Bar Graph") 
plt.show() 
 
 
 
 
2) Creating a horizontal bar chart 
SOURCE CODE: 
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt 
y= ['one','two','three','four','five'] 
x = [5,24,35,67,12] 
plt.barh(y,x) 
plt.ylabel("Pen sold") 
plt.xlabel("Price") 
plt.title("Horizontal barGraph") 
plt.show()

3) Write a Python program to create a pie chart of the popularity of programming 
languages. 
SOURCE CODE: 
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt 
l='Java','Python','PHP','JavaScript','C#','C++' 
p=[22.2,17.6,8.8,8,7.7,6.7] 
c=["#1f77b4","#ff7f0e","#2ca02c","#d62728","#9467bd","#8c564b"] 
e=(0.1,0,0,0,0,0) 
plt.pie(p,explode=e,labels=l,colors=c,autopct='%1.1f%%',shadow=True,startangle=140) 
